# Module 12 – Active Directory
{"module_id":12,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"Write the bloodhound-python command to collect all AD data from corp.local (DC: 10.10.10.5) as user 'john:Pass123', using the DC as DNS server:","options":None,"answer":"bloodhound-python -d corp.local -u john -p Pass123 -dc 10.10.10.5 -c All -ns 10.10.10.5","explanation":"bloodhound-python runs collection from Linux without domain join. -c All collects all data types. -ns sets DNS to the DC (required for proper LDAP connectivity). Output is a ZIP importable into BloodHound.","validation_regex":"bloodhound-python.*-d.*corp\\.local.*-c All?.*-ns","hints":["-ns sets DNS server to the DC","-c All collects all data types"]},
